title the voice ships, a document gets two homes, and the shed list comes back empty
prompt Keaton asked to close two reds, then across several mid-turn messages: seat xy as speeddial, ship context/KYRI.md in the seed, brix-infuse Tablecloth and Gauge into the root README, crawl every recursive markdown leaf from the README, decide whether the %NNN REDS pattern should become chronological marks, write a first-hour SHOPPING guide, and silo a browse of 39 active-designing documents with a shed proof.
think Closed the two reds first. pool_isolation was genuine drift -- table.add_child renamed add_dependent five weeks ago, two call sites, builds and passes five isolation claims.
think pond_ring_lantern was filed as the same fault and was not. It builds a Wayland terminal on a pier with no libwayland-client or libxkbcommon on any linker path. Corrected the %171 record rather than leaving a wrong row standing.
think The build script had printed "assuming host link seams on metal" and handed that guess to a compile that discovered the truth at link time -- the same shape %172 retired hours earlier. Replaced the guess with tools/fixtures/display_seam_probe.sh, which searches what the LINKER searches rather than the filesystem, since /nix/store holds libwayland-client.so.0.25.0 and Zig still refused.
think Proved the gate from the open side as hard as the shut side: stub seams on LIBRARY_PATH let the build reach compile, and its ordinary failure exits non-3. A gate proven only shut cannot be told from a bypass.
think Caught my own bug inside the fix: the probe call was an unguarded command substitution under set -e, so the script died at the assignment printing no explanation -- the gate silently doing the thing the gate exists to prevent.
think The next roster run then found %174, which is mine from the prior commit: I ran the roster, read 31 of 31 green, THEN git add -A, which swept tools/glow/.cache and two pre-fold dangling symlinks into main. Stage first, then measure.
think On the %NNN question I measured before arguing: 2,519 citations tree-wide, 532 inside commit messages and 208 in dated testimony, both beyond any migration. And the rows already carry stamp and name, so a conversion would remove the number rather than add chronology.
think The deciding distinction is forecast versus census. Every example the mark law gives is a plan that announced a length and stopped short. A red's number counts what happened and cannot come out wrong, and its gapless spine proves the record is whole where a stamp cannot.
think Declined the standfast and said why in one line: the same lap's crawl found 112 broken links across 42 living documents, which newcomers read, while row numbering is read by the ledger's own guard.
think For KYRI.md the instruction met a seated safeguard -- the seed's NO_PERSONAL gate against seven Keaton references. Depersonalized in place per the acme-employee-voice rule rather than forking a variant, and named the three withheld siblings in prose rather than linking them.
think Keaton offered ember/voices/ then answered his own question better: one document, several homes, proven identical, declared in Brix. Built that, which dissolves the placement question entirely -- a home is a declaration rather than a move.
think Recorded the naming collision in the descriptor rather than swallowing it: Ember is itself one of the four voices Kyri carries, so ember/voices/ is a room named after one of its own contents.
think The seed-link guard caught me shipping a phantom tablecloth/ link into the front door -- a directory this tree has never had, in the same class this whole session has been retiring.
think On the 39-document shed list, measurement answered plainly: all 39 present, all 39 cited, floor 3 and ceiling 46. None shed-ready, and the honest read is that the browse is the weave's spine rather than its overgrowth.
obs Every one of the day's reds now lives in the measuring equipment or in the tree's description of itself, and this lap added two of my own to that count -- %174 from staging order, and the set -e swallow inside the gate.
obs Left named rather than started: the fascia weave over seven clusters (a living index page per cluster, not edits into dated bodies), the 112 living broken links, and Door front pages for Caravan and Mycelium.
